-- mod-bleakhold-ui: the café's world templates (protocol section 21): The Lion's Roast (Stormwind) and The
-- Grinding Tusk (Orgrimmar). Generated by Tools/CafeForge/cafeforge_data.py from Tools/CafeForge/cafe.json; do
-- not edit. The file owns whole id ranges (gameobject and creature templates 909300-909379, items
-- 909380-909389, npc_text 909300-909319, spell_custom_attr 100900-100959): each is deleted before its rows are
-- inserted, so the file can be applied again (ac-db-import re-runs it when it changes).
-- The pieces are placed in game with .cafe build; nothing here spawns anything. The café spells (spell_dbc
-- 100900-100959) and the new art's GameObjectDisplayInfo rows come from CafeForge on the server; until they are
-- there the module keeps the café off (spells) or uses the stand-ins (art).

-- gameobject_template: 909300-909323 the new-art pieces (display = entry - 890000, patch-4.MPQ), 909330-909353
-- their stand-ins on stock displays (entry + 30, the same name), 909360-909379 furniture and the .cafe show
-- markers. GENERIC (5) pieces show their name on hover (Data0 floating tooltip, Data1 highlight); chairs (7)
-- have Data0 slots and Data1 height.
DELETE FROM `gameobject_template` WHERE `entry` BETWEEN 909300 AND 909379;
